/-
# A free normal subgroup of the Artin group of type D₄ (Kourovka Notebook Problem 8.11)

Kourovka Notebook, Problem 8.11 (D. L. Johnson), marked solved in the 21st issue: consider the group
`M = ⟨x, y, z, t | [x, y] = [y, z] = [z, x] = (x, t) = (y, t) = (z, t) = 1⟩`, where `[x, y] =
x⁻¹y⁻¹xy` and `(x, t) = x⁻¹t⁻¹x⁻¹txt`. The subgroup `H = ⟨x, t, y⟩` is isomorphic to the braid group
`B₄`, and is normally complemented by `N = ⟨(zx⁻¹)^M⟩`. Is `N` a free group (?) of countably
infinite rank (?) on which `H` acts faithfully by conjugation?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.PresentedGroup

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ArtinD4FreeNormalSubgroupKourovka8Problem11Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 8.11 (D. L. Johnson). UnsolvedMath record
UM-00700463 (`KOU-8.11`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

`M` is Mathlib's `PresentedGroup` on `x, y, z, t = of 0, of 1, of 2, of 3` with the six relators as
printed; `N` is the normal closure of `z x⁻¹` and `H` the subgroup generated by `x, t, y`. The three
questions marked (?) are three targets: `N` is free, of rank `3` (answering the first); `N` is free
of countably infinite rank (refuted); `H` acts faithfully on `N` by conjugation (only `1`
centralizes `N`).
-/

/-- The generators `x, y, z, t` of the free group on four letters. -/
abbrev genX : FreeGroup (Fin 4) := FreeGroup.of 0
/-- The generator `y`. -/
abbrev genY : FreeGroup (Fin 4) := FreeGroup.of 1
/-- The generator `z`. -/
abbrev genZ : FreeGroup (Fin 4) := FreeGroup.of 2
/-- The generator `t`. -/
abbrev genT : FreeGroup (Fin 4) := FreeGroup.of 3

/-- The relators of `M = ⟨x, y, z, t | [x, y] = [y, z] = [z, x] = (x, t) = (y, t) = (z, t) = 1⟩`,
with `[u, v] = u⁻¹v⁻¹uv` and `(u, t) = u⁻¹t⁻¹u⁻¹tut`. -/
def artinRelators : Set (FreeGroup (Fin 4)) :=
  {genX⁻¹ * genY⁻¹ * genX * genY, genY⁻¹ * genZ⁻¹ * genY * genZ, genZ⁻¹ * genX⁻¹ * genZ * genX,
    genX⁻¹ * genT⁻¹ * genX⁻¹ * genT * genX * genT, genY⁻¹ * genT⁻¹ * genY⁻¹ * genT * genY * genT,
    genZ⁻¹ * genT⁻¹ * genZ⁻¹ * genT * genZ * genT}

/-- The group `M` (the Artin group of type `D₄`). -/
abbrev artinGroupM : Type := PresentedGroup artinRelators

/-- The subgroup `N`: the normal closure of `z x⁻¹` in `M`. -/
def subgroupN : Subgroup artinGroupM :=
  Subgroup.normalClosure {PresentedGroup.of 2 * (PresentedGroup.of 0)⁻¹}

/-- The subgroup `H = ⟨x, t, y⟩` of `M`. -/
def subgroupH : Subgroup artinGroupM :=
  Subgroup.closure {PresentedGroup.of 0, PresentedGroup.of 3, PresentedGroup.of 1}

/-- Kourovka 8.11 (D. L. Johnson), freeness and rank: `N` is a free group (of rank `3`). -/
def subgroupNFreeOfRankThree : Prop := Nonempty (subgroupN ≃* FreeGroup (Fin 3))

/-- Kourovka 8.11 (D. L. Johnson), the rank asked for: `N` is free of countably infinite rank. -/
def subgroupNFreeOfCountableRank : Prop := Nonempty (subgroupN ≃* FreeGroup ℕ)

/-- Kourovka 8.11 (D. L. Johnson), the action: `H` acts faithfully on `N` by conjugation. -/
def subgroupHActsFaithfully : Prop :=
  ∀ h ∈ subgroupH, (∀ n ∈ subgroupN, h * n * h⁻¹ = n) → h = 1

/--
Resolved true: the 21st issue marks 8.11 solved: as Antolín pointed out, `M` is the Artin group of
type `D₄`, and Perron and Vannier (1996) proved that `N` is a free group of rank `3`. Source: E. I.
Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 8.11 (D. L. Johnson); resolution: B. Perron and J. P.
Vannier, Groupe de monodromie géométrique des singularités simples, Math. Ann. 306 (1996), 231-245;
remark of Y. Antolín, Kourovka Notebook 21st issue, Problem 8.11, marked solved: M is the Artin
group of type D₄; N is a free group of rank 3 and H acts on N faithfully by conjugation (Perron and
Vannier); paper, Corollaire 1 (semidirect product of a free group of rank n - 1 by the braid group
B_n) and Théorème 1 (faithfulness), as quoted in Crisp and Paris, arXiv:math/0210438, Propositions
2.3 and 2.5, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01445249.
-/
public theorem_wanted subgroupNFreeOfRankThree_holds : subgroupNFreeOfRankThree

/--
Resolved false: the 21st issue marks 8.11 solved: by Perron and Vannier (1996) `N` is free of rank
`3`, not of countably infinite rank. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 8.11
(D. L. Johnson); resolution: B. Perron and J. P. Vannier, Groupe de monodromie géométrique des
singularités simples, Math. Ann. 306 (1996), 231-245; remark of Y. Antolín, Kourovka Notebook 21st
issue, Problem 8.11, marked solved: M is the Artin group of type D₄; N is a free group of rank 3 and
H acts on N faithfully by conjugation (Perron and Vannier); paper, Corollaire 1 (semidirect product
of a free group of rank n - 1 by the braid group B_n) and Théorème 1 (faithfulness), as quoted in
Crisp and Paris, arXiv:math/0210438, Propositions 2.3 and 2.5, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01445249.
-/
public theorem_wanted subgroupNFreeOfCountableRank_refuted : ¬ subgroupNFreeOfCountableRank

/--
Resolved true: the 21st issue marks 8.11 solved: by Perron and Vannier (1996) `H` acts on `N`
faithfully by conjugation. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Problem 8.11 (D. L.
Johnson); resolution: B. Perron and J. P. Vannier, Groupe de monodromie géométrique des singularités
simples, Math. Ann. 306 (1996), 231-245; remark of Y. Antolín, Kourovka Notebook 21st issue, Problem
8.11, marked solved: M is the Artin group of type D₄; N is a free group of rank 3 and H acts on N
faithfully by conjugation (Perron and Vannier); paper, Corollaire 1 (semidirect product of a free
group of rank n - 1 by the braid group B_n) and Théorème 1 (faithfulness), as quoted in Crisp and
Paris, arXiv:math/0210438, Propositions 2.3 and 2.5, https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01445249.
-/
public theorem_wanted subgroupHActsFaithfully_holds : subgroupHActsFaithfully

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.ArtinD4FreeNormalSubgroupKourovka8Problem11Wanted
